"Enough!"
{n}As soon as the Horned Hunter's body disappears in the fire, the destroyed throne room is flooded with light. The {g|LanternKing}Lantern King{/g}, in his true blazing form, appears in the middle of the room. His furious mask is ringed by fire. The games have ended.
Time freezes like resin, trapping you and the {g|Eldest}Eldest{/g} in amber light. And this light grows brighter...{/n}

756d5388-90d1-4e11-863a-c2f9048bef94:
{n}Nok-Nok follows your gesture, and as he turns...
...but already unsteady, he twists and falls again, collapsing to the ground – the drumming falls awkwardly silent with a few gasps, then laughing from the goblins.
To his credit, Nok-Nok picks himself up and dusts himself off, then the drumming resumes. He's giving a half-smile, as if he's not certain of his own success.{/n}

cc0a6bb3-98b2-4591-9140-e4d3c1a6357c:
"You must guess what it is. The {g|LanternKing}Lantern King{/g} loves masks. Since ancient times he's wandered the planes, assuming the forms of the most unique and unusual creatures. But his own masks are something more. Each of them holds a fraction of his essence."
{n}Magdh's voice becomes dull, as if she is sinking into memory.{/n}
"He made this mask long ago, when he was young, as was all {g|First World}the First World{/g}. And, as with many early creations, its author disapproved of it. It betrayed too much compassion, a quality that annoyed the young demigod."

75af4f44-e3eb-4a59-bf33-3122e461def8:
{n}And for this brief moment, you look into the abyss that hides behind the name {g|LanternKing}'Lantern King'{/g}. And what is there? Light? Laughter? Bolts of lightning — or thoughts of an ancient mind, mighty and strange? You haven't the time to comprehend all you see, but you know one thing for true. The Lantern King is cursed.
The Lantern King is mortal. The punishment he heaped upon Nyrissa has returned to him, and taken his precious immortality.
It is your turn to speak!{/n}

320c0a40-6312-45a4-8b33-d8ce0cabe425:
{n}You seem to hear thunder rumble in the distance. The nymph turns to leave, but suddenly raises her eyes to you and speaks again:{/n} "Do you know why I couldn't immediately recognize the intrusion, when you and the foolish little robin bard broke into my dreams?
Because it wasn't the first time I dreamt of you, {name}."
{n}With these words, the nymph's silhouette dissolves into thin air.{/n}

aaf2a663-ae3a-4c65-a712-4f19846a8a6f:
{n}The shamans words become quieter and quieter.{/n} "We be {g|Lamashtu}Lamashtu's{/g} sons... watering... seed-sowing... readying... for the season… of Bloom... All together... boom... boom... boom..."
{n}The shaman emits a long wheeze and freezes, looking straight into your eyes. His dull eyes are lit by an evil flicker.{/n}
"The season of Bloom has begun. You no stop us."
